    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now reverse the weighted average.\n\n2 kg at ₹12 and 3 kg at ₹x make a mixture worth ₹18.\n\nTotal mixture cost = 5×18 = ₹90.\nKnown cost = 2×12 = ₹24.\nSo 3x = 90−24 = 66.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "x = 66÷3 = ₹22/kg.\n\nThis method is direct: target total value minus known total value leaves the missing component's total value.\n\nThen divide by its quantity.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
