    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "You can also find a missing price from a ratio.\n\n₹10 and ₹x are mixed in ratio 2:3 to make ₹16.\n\n2×10 + 3x = 5×16\n20 + 3x = 80\n3x = 60.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So x = ₹20.\n\nThis is the same weighted-average equation, just solved backwards.\n\nA quick check: ₹16 lies between ₹10 and ₹20 and is closer to ₹20 because more of ₹20 is used.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
